# Slot 5 (Calibrated Confidence, Physics, excess, standard) — review log

## 2026-04-10 cycle 11 — fact pack curation

**Fact pack written:** `corpus/fact-packs/09-physics-thermal-conductivity-extrapolation-01.md`

**Scenario design rationale:** Thermal conductivity of a novel ceramic-polymer composite. Three independent room-temperature methods (laser flash, hot-wire, guarded hot-plate) converge on ~4.0–4.3 W/m·K within stated uncertainties — textbook strong-evidence claim. A theoretical model (effective medium theory) predicts temperature-dependent decline to ~2.8 W/m·K at 500°C. A single 300°C measurement (one method, 3× wider uncertainty) is consistent with the model but does not strongly constrain it. The application target is 500°C, 200°C beyond any measured data. This scenario maps directly to the "I know / I believe / I suspect" sub-facet — "know" the room-temp value, "believe" the model form, "suspect" the 500°C prediction.

